    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d159">

                <pb facs="0179" n="167" sameAs="frus:frus1943v05/pg167"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">825.24/954: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Ambassador in Chile</hi>
                        (<hi rendition="#italic">Bowers</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1943-04-06T19:00:00-04:00">April 6, 1943—7 p.m.</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>403. Your A–364 of March 11.<anchor n="92" xml:id="d159-f1"/> Please urge Chilean
                    authorities to announce immediately to the trade the list of non-importable
                    articles, <pb facs="0180" n="168" xml:id="pg168"/> in accordance with Henry’s
                    and Wilkinson’s understanding that this would be done. In fairness to United
                    States exporters it is desired to publish the list here at once, but
                    announcement by the Chilean Government should take place previously or
                    coincidently. Telegraph reply.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
